    <bpmn:process id="W_W490" name="W490. Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Investigation &amp; Task Force" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Pattern detection from EBR analytics (W466); law enforcement tip; multi-store incident correlation; industry ORC alert
Frequency: Event-driven (investigation activation); monthly (task force review); quarterly (industry coordination)
Volume: ~5–10 active ORC investigations/year; monthly task force meetings
Owner: Loss Prevention Director
Participants: LP Investigators, Store Managers, Regional Managers, VP Legal, Security Lead, PNP/CIDG, Industry ORC Alliance
Source: workflow W490 — Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Investigation &amp; Task Force</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W490_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W490_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W490_Lane2" name="LP Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W490_Lane3" name="LP Investigator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W490_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W490_Start5" name="Pattern detection from EBR analytics (W466); law enforcement tip; multi-store incident…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task6" name="Pattern Detection &amp; Intelligence Gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pattern Detection &amp; Intelligence Gathering: LP Analyst identifies ORC patterns from multiple data sources: (a) EBR exception reports (W466) — correlated voids, returns, and inventory shortages across multiple stores; (b) inventory shrinkage reports (W248) — stores with abnormal shrinkage spikes; (c) return transaction analysis — high-frequency returns across stores with similar merchandise, same customer IDs; (d) POS exception data — transactions involving same SKUs repeatedly at different stores; (e) external intelligence — industry ORC alerts from Philippine Retailers Association (PRA), local law enforcement bulletins; (f) social media monitoring for resale of stolen BuildRight merchandise (Facebook Marketplace, Lazada, Shopee)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task7" name="Case File Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Case File Creation: LP Director creates ORC case file: (a) case number, classification (organized shoplifting, return fraud, employee collusion, cargo theft, vendor fraud); (b) suspected ring profile (number of individuals, vehicles, stores targeted); (c) financial impact estimate (total known losses from correlated incidents); (d) scope: affected stores, regions, time period; (e) assign lead LP Investigator; (f) classify confidentiality level (ORC investigations are strictly confidential to avoid tipping off suspects)
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–4 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task8" name="Cross-Store Investigation Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cross-Store Investigation Coordination: LP Investigator coordinates investigation across affected stores: (a) pull CCTV footage from all affected stores (W71) — look for common individuals, vehicles, methods; (b) correlate POS transaction data across stores — identify common payment methods, loyalty accounts, or patterns; (c) interview Store Managers and relevant staff confidentially; (d) cross-reference employee work schedules (W34) against incident times (for employee collusion cases); (e) coordinate with DC LP for cargo theft cases (verify seal integrity, GPS tracking per W199)
Responsible (R): LP Investigator
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: 1–3 weeks/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task9" name="Evidence Compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evidence Compilation: LP Investigator compiles prosecution-ready evidence package: (a) chronological incident timeline across all affected stores; (b) CCTV footage compilation (edited highlights with timestamps); (c) POS transaction records (certified system extracts); (d) inventory shrinkage documentation (W248/W92); (e) employee statements (notarized if necessary); (f) financial impact quantification; (g) social media screenshots of suspected resale activity (with metadata preservation per Data Privacy Act W271)
Responsible (R): LP Investigator
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 3–5 days/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task10" name="Law Enforcement Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Law Enforcement Coordination: LP Director coordinates with law enforcement for criminal prosecution: (a) for non-employee suspects: file complaint with PNP Criminal Investigation and Detection Group (CIDG) or local PNP station; (b) for employee suspects: coordinate with VP Legal and HR for parallel criminal and administrative proceedings (DOLE due process per W43); (c) for cargo theft: coordinate with PNP Highway Patrol Group and port security; (d) provide evidence package to law enforcement; (e) assist in entrapment/buy-bust operations if requested by law enforcement; (f) attend court hearings as prosecution witness
Responsible (R): LP Director / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task11" name="ORC Task Force Monthly Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: ORC Task Force Monthly Review: LP Director chairs monthly ORC Task Force meeting: (a) review all active ORC cases and investigation status; (b) review new intelligence and pattern alerts; (c) assess financial impact of ORC losses vs. period; (d) coordinate with Regional Managers on store-level prevention measures; (e) review and update ORC prevention strategies (EAS tag placement, high-value item display security, return policy adjustments); (f) coordinate with IT on EBR rule enhancements (W466)
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task12" name="Industry Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Industry Coordination: LP Director participates in industry ORC coordination: (a) attend quarterly Philippine Retailers Association (PRA) ORC working group meetings; (b) share non-confidential intelligence (modus operandi, known suspect profiles, vehicle descriptions) with peer retailers; (c) coordinate with competing hardware retailers on common ORC threats; (d) contribute to industry-wide ORC database (if available)
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W490_Task13" name="Case Closure &amp; Lessons Learned">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Case Closure &amp; Lessons Learned: Upon case resolution: (a) LP Director prepares case closure report: total financial loss, recovery amount, criminal prosecution outcome, employees terminated, policy changes implemented; (b) conduct lessons learned session with affected stores; (c) update LP procedures and EBR rules (W466) to prevent recurrence; (d) update ORC intelligence database for future pattern recognition; (e) report outcome to VP Store Operations and CFO
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 days/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W490_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W490_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W490_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W490_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-306 (ensure controlled execution — Specialized Audit Domains (PA-21.3).) | - operational: Loss Prevention Director review and approval gate
Owner: Loss Prevention Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W490_Assoc16" sourceRef="W490_Annotation15" targetRef="W490_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W490_Flow17" sourceRef="W490_Start5" targetRef="W490_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W490_Flow18" sourceRef="W490_Task6" targetRef="W490_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W490_Flow19" sourceRef="W490_Task7" targetRef="W490_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W490_Flow20" sourceRef="W490_Task8" targetRef="W490_Task9" />
